The correct solution is to add a catch block for FileNotFoundException to handle the case where the file does not exist.

**Step 4: Provide a code snippet that demonstrates the correct solution.**

Here is a code snippet that demonstrates the correct solution:

```java
import java.io.*;

public class FileTest {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            File file = new File("data.txt");
            Scanner scanner = new Scanner(file);
            while(scanner.hasNext()) {
                System.out.println(scanner.next());
            }
        } catch (FileNotFoundException e) {
            System.out.println("File does not exist.");
        }
    }
}
```

